/-!
# On projective space, finite total `Hom` from the twists forces perfectness

Let `k` be a field and `X = ℙⁿ_k`. An object `M` of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` such that
`∑_i dim_k Hom(𝒪(-a), M[i]) < ∞` for `a = 0, …, n` is perfect.

This is the projective-space step of [Stacks, Tag 0FYD] and the implication (3) ⇒ (1) of
[Stacks, Tag 0FYB], whose proof in the source passes through the equivalence of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)`
with the derived category of the Beilinson algebra. Here the full exceptional sequence
`𝒪(-n), …, 𝒪(-1), 𝒪` is used directly
(`CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.prop_of_hasFiniteTotalHom_of_exceptional`):

* each `𝒪(d)` is exceptional — its endomorphisms are the scalars
  (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistEndomorphisms.exists_eq_smul_id_twistObj`) and it has no
  higher self-extensions (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistExt.subsingleton_hom_twist_shift_of_le`,
  from [Stacks, Tag 01XT]);
* the sequence is semi-orthogonal, again by [Stacks, Tag 01XT];
* `Hom(𝒪(d), 𝒪(e)[i])` is finite dimensional;
* the sequence generates `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)`: by the Koszul complex of [Stacks, Tag 0BQS] every
  `𝒪(-m)`, `m ≥ 0`, lies in the subcategory generated by the sequence ([Stacks, Tag 0A9V]), and
  the negative twists generate
  (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistGeneration.isZero_of_subsingleton_hom_twist`, the derived form of
  [Stacks, Tag 0BQR]).

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpacePerfect.isPerfect_of_hasFiniteTotalHom_twist`.
-/

-- This file uses the locally small derived-category models below, which are not
-- global instances (see `StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedCategory.LocallySmall`):
-- `D(𝒪_X)` for a scheme.
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated
